        "original_id": "25866683-9ccb-5f52-ad3c-dd561e87fff9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels, Lock, Stock...\n- People: Guy Ritchie, Matthew Vaughn, Jason Flemyng, Dexter Fletcher, Nick Moran, Jason Statham, Steven Mackintosh, Vinnie Jones, Sting\n- Roles: actor, professional footballer, midfielder\n- Organizations: Wimbledon, Leeds United, Sheffield United, Chelsea, Wales\n\nFacts:\n- Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels is a 1998 British crime comedy film written and directed by Guy Ritchie and produced by Matthew Vaughn.\n- Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels stars an ensemble cast featuring Jason Flemyng, Dexter Fletcher, Nick Moran, Jason Statham, Steven Mackintosh, Vinnie Jones, and Sting.\n- Vincent Peter \"Vinnie\" Jones was born on 5 January 1965 and is a British actor and former professional footballer.\n- Vinnie Jones played as a midfielder from 1984 to 1999, notably for Wimbledon, Leeds United, Sheffield United, Chelsea, and Wales.\n- Lock, Stock... is a 2000 television series that is an offshoot of the 1998 film Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
